{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cluster tree visitor pattern cluster tree visitor pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md","fileName":"Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 22:06\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C++ Clustering Design Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Clustering Design Patterns","dataclusteringincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cluster tree visitor pattern cluster tree visitor pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md","fileName":"Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern","heading":"Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Visitor pattern moves operations on a node hierarchy into a separate class family. Each leaf or internal node accepts a NodeVisitor and dispatches to the overload matching its concrete node type.\n\nClusLib uses visitors to collect join values, build flat partitions, and draw dendrograms without embedding every operation in Node. Adding a new visitor is easy, while adding a new node type requires changing the visitor interface and each concrete visitor.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Clustering Design Patterns","dataclusteringincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tree Visitor Pattern.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cluster Tr